{"type":"text","timestamp":1786327615505,"sessionID":"ses_01694d34cffeYFw5xwaTPO3h5H","part":{"id":"prt_fe96c4332001danlV045MdeLv4","messageID":"msg_fe96c3a11001OIxynqoHnKXkvH","sessionID":"ses_01694d34cffeYFw5xwaTPO3h5H","type":"text","text":"Per the evidence formula `Percentage of Increase = (consumption2013 - consumption2012) / consumption2013 * 100%`, computed per segment (EUR only):\n\n- **SME**: 88.02% — biggest increase\n- **KAM**: 84.69%\n- **LAM**: 84.37% — lowest increase\n\nFinal Answer: Biggest increase = SME (88.02%); lowest increase = LAM (84.37%)\nEvidence SQL: SELECT c.Segment, CAST((SUM(CASE WHEN substr(y.Date,1,4)='2013' THEN y.Consumption END) - SUM(CASE WHEN substr(y.Date,1,4)='2012' THEN y.Consumption END)) AS REAL) / SUM(CASE WHEN substr(y.Date,1,4)='2013' THEN y.Consumption END) * 100 AS pct_increase FROM yearmonth y JOIN customers c ON y.CustomerID=c.CustomerID WHERE c.Segment IN ('SME','LAM','KAM') AND c.Currency='EUR' GROUP BY c.Segment ORDER BY pct_increase DESC","time":{"start":1786327614258,"end":1786327615491}}}
